        "flightIncluded": false,
        "flights_included": false,
        "location": "Spiti Valley",
        "routeSummary": "with Chandratal Lake",
        "overviewText": "Step into the wild heart of the Himalayas with the **Spiti Valley tour** — a remote mountain destination where time slows, skies stretch wider, and every turn reveals stories carved in ancient monasteries, whispering winds, and crystal-clear alpine lakes. \n\nFrom the charming solitude of **[Chitkul village](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chitkul)**, India’s last inhabited village, to the colorful prayer flags fluttering over the historic **[Tabo monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tabo-monastery)** and vibrant **[Kaza town](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kaza)**, and the surreal turquoise waters of **Chandrataal Lake** at 14,000 feet, this journey offers a soul-stirring escape into raw, untouched natural beauty. Nestle into cozy local homestays, savor authentic rustic Himachali cuisine, and connect with a lively group of fellow travelers sharing the adventure. \n\nBeginning and ending in Delhi, this **7-day, 6-night Spiti Valley road trip** is your gateway to the unfiltered magic of Himachal Pradesh’s most remote paradise.\n\n### **Tour Details Summary**\n\n**Duration:** 7 Days / 6 Nights\n\n**Start Point:** Delhi (ISBT Kashmiri Gate) by Volvo Bus\n\n**End Point:** Delhi by Volvo Bus via Manali\n\n**Route:** Delhi → Shimla → Chitkul → Nako → Tabo → Dhankar → Kaza → Key, Komic, Langza, Hikkim → Kibber & Chicham Bridge → Chandrataal → Manali → Delhi\n\n**Transport:** AC Volvo Bus (Delhi–Shimla & Manali–Delhi), Tempo Traveller for Spiti road journey\n\n**Accommodation:** Hotels, homestays, and tents/camps (especially near Chandrataal Lake)\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast & Dinner included; Lunch and meals during transit excluded\n\n**Highlights:** India’s last inhabited village: Chitkul, [Ancient Tabo Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tabo-monastery) & cliff-top Dhankar Gompa, Highest post office (Hikkim) and motorable village ([Komic](https://indiatour.live/attractions/komic)). Asia’s highest suspension bridge at Chicham, Magical blue waters of Chandrataal (Moon Lake), High-altitude desert landscapes, fossil hunting, and Tibetan culture, Scenic drives through Spiti Valley, [Kunzum La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kunzum-pass) & [Atal Tunnel](https://indiatour.live/attractions/atal-tunnel)\n\n**Inclusions:** AC Volvo bus tickets, Tempo Traveler for internal travel, accommodation on a sharing basis, meals as mentioned, permits, sightseeing, trip leader, and 24x7 support\n\n**Exclusions:** 5% GST, lunch, meals during bus/train journeys, adventure activities, personal expenses, and additional costs due to road closures or weather\n\n### **Who Should Book This Spiti Valley Tour**\n### \n- Backpackers and budget-conscious travelers seeking a group road trip\n- Anyone who’s dreamt of [Chandrataal](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake), Key Monastery, or sending a postcard from [Hikkim](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hikkim)!\n- Solo travelers wanting to meet like-minded explorers and discover Spiti together\n- Couples, friends, and small groups looking for a private, well-curated Spiti Valley tour—complete with train travel, meals, permits, and local transport, all managed end-to-end\n- Culture enthusiasts and spiritual travelers looking to explore Spiti Valley’s Tibetan Buddhist heritage, ancient monasteries, and high-altitude Himalayan villages\n- Photography enthusiasts wanting to capture frozen waterfalls, snowy landscapes, and remote monasteries\n- First-time visitors wanting a hassle-free winter trip to Spiti\n- Travelers comfortable with cold weather and rugged mountain roads\n\n### **Top Destinations Covered in This Spiti Valley Group Trip**\n### \n\n*  **Shimla:** Kick off your Spiti Valley adventure from [Shimla](https://indiatour.live/attractions/shimla), the charming colonial hill town that serves as the gateway to Kinnaur and Spiti. Known for its pine forests, winding mountain roads, and scenic vistas, Shimla offers the perfect blend of comfort and altitude to begin your high-altitude journey.\n\n*  **Chitkul:** Tucked away in the Kinnaur district, Chitkul is the last inhabited village on the Indo-Tibet border. Surrounded by snow-clad peaks and the Baspa River, this hamlet offers raw Himalayan beauty and local charm. The wooden houses, traditional Kinnauri culture, and postcard-perfect settings make [Chitkul](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chitkul) a photographer’s dream.\n\n* **Tabo:** Often called the ‘Ajanta of the Himalayas’, [Tabo Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tabo-monastery) is one of the oldest functioning Buddhist enclaves in the world. Explore ancient murals, mud-walled caves, and peaceful prayer halls as you soak in the spiritual vibe of this high-altitude village.\n\n*  **[Dhankar](https://indiatour.live/attractions/dhankar-monastery):** Dhankar, perched dramatically on a cliff between Tabo and Kaza, is known for its fortress-like monastery and panoramic views of the confluence of the Spiti and Pin Rivers. A must-visit for those who love remote monasteries with a story to tell.\n\n* **Kaza:** Kaza is the largest town in Spiti Valley and your base for exploring the region’s remote villages and monasteries. This vibrant Himalayan town is dotted with cafes, local markets, and traditional homestays. It’s where ancient culture meets youthful travel vibes.\n\n* **Key Monastery:** Key Gompa is the largest and most photographed monastery in Spiti Valley. Set on a hill overlooking the Spiti River, it’s a treasure trove of Buddhist art, thangkas, and ancient scriptures. The view from the top is unmatched.\n\n* **[Komic](https://indiatour.live/attractions/komic):** Sitting at an altitude of over 15,000 ft, Komic is the highest motorable village in the world. Explore its tiny monastery, interact with locals, and experience life at extreme altitudes. Don’t forget to get your altitude selfie!\n\n* **Langza:** Langza is famous for its fossil-rich soil and the towering Buddha statue that faces the Himalayan peaks. It's a place where geology, spirituality, and unmatched landscapes meet. You might even find a fossil to take home (ethically)!\n\n* **[Hikkim](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hikkim):** At 14,400 ft, Hikkim houses the highest post office in the world. Drop a handwritten postcard to loved ones and experience how life functions in one of the most remote villages on the planet.\n\n*  **Kibber:** Kibber is one of the highest inhabited villages in India, often visited for its stunning views, proximity to the [Kibber Wildlife Sanctuary](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kibber), and traditional stone houses.\n\n*  **[Chicham Bridge](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chicham-bridge):** Connecting Kibber and Chicham villages, this architectural marvel stands tall over a deep gorge, offering a thrilling experience and panoramic mountain views.\n\n* **[Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake):** Chandrataal is one of the most iconic high-altitude lakes in the Himalayas. Located at over 14,000 ft, this crescent-shaped lake changes colors with the sky and is a haven for stargazing and soul-soothing silence.\n\n* **Manali:** End your trip in Manali with some adrenaline-packed activities like paragliding and river rafting, followed by café hopping in Old Manali and souvenir shopping at [Mall Road](https://indiatour.live/attractions/mall-road-market-manali).",
