      "overviewText": "This Spiti Valley Road Trip is your ticket to an offbeat Himalayan escape—where snow-laden villages, ancient monasteries, and high mountain passes reveal the untouched soul of the cold desert. \n\nExplore the best of Spiti—[Shimla](https://indiatour.live/attractions/shimla), Chitkul, [Kalpa](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kalpa), Nako, Tabo, Kaza, [Key Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/key-monastery), Chicham Bridge, and the surreal [Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake). Each stop adds a new layer of thrill, peace, or wonder.\nThis tour includes comfortable homestays, hotels, local meals, and full logistics so you can focus on the experience—not the planning.\n\nTravelers can join us from Ahmedabad (via train) or Delhi—and yes, anyone from any part of the country can hop on from Delhi.\n\n### Tour Details Summary\n\n**Duration:** 11 Days / 10 Nights (Ahemdabad), 7 Days / 6 Nights (Delhi)\n\n**Start Point:** Ahmedabad (Gandhinagar) by Train / Delhi\n\n**End Point:** Ahmedabad by Train via Chandigarh / Delhi\n\n**Ahmedabad Route:** Ahmedabad → Chandigarh → Shimla → Chitkul → Nako → Tabo → Dhankar → Kaza → Key, Komic, Hikkim, Langza → Kibber, Chicham → Chandrataal → Manali → Chandigarh → Ahmedabad\n\n**Delhi Route:** Delhi → Shimla → [Chitkul](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chitkul) → Nako → Tabo → Dhankar → Kaza → Key, Komic, Hikkim, Langza → Kibber, Chicham → Chandrataal → Manali → Delhi\n\n**Transport:** Train (Ahmedabad–Chandigarh–Ahmedabad), tempo traveller/taxi for road travel, internal Volvo bus (for Delhi package)\n\n**Accommodation:** Hotels, homestays, and campsites on a sharing basis\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast & Dinner included; food during travel excluded\n\n**Highlights:** Shimla, the untouched beauty of [Chitkul](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chitkul) (last Indian village), spiritual visits to Tabo & [Dhankar](https://indiatour.live/attractions/dhankar-monastery) monasteries, high-altitude marvels like Key, Komic, Langza & Hikkim, Chicham Bridge (Asia’s highest), mystical Chandratal Lake, adventurous drive through [Atal Tunnel](https://indiatour.live/attractions/atal-tunnel), and Manali sightseeing with adventure sports\n\n**Inclusions:** Round-trip train tickets (Ahmedabad–Chandigarh), private road trip transport, accommodation, meals as per itinerary, Volvo bus tickets (Delhi package), sightseeing, taxes, parking, inner line permits, trip leader, 24x7 support, first-aid assistance\n\n**Exclusions:** 5% GST, lunch & food during travel, 2-sharing stay upgrade (available as add-on), and any additional costs due to roadblocks, weather delays, or personal expenses\n\n### Who Should Book This Spiti Valley Road Trip\n\n- Flexible start options available for travelers to join from Ahmedabad (train) or Delhi\n- Backpackers and budget-conscious travelers seeking a group road trip\n- Travelers who want to experience **[Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake) camping** and **high-altitude Spiti villages**\n- Anyone who wants to cover **Spiti Valley’s must-visit places** in a short duration\n- Solo travelers wanting to meet like-minded explorers and discover Spiti together\n- Couples, friends, and small groups looking for a private, well-curated Spiti Valley tour—complete with train travel, meals, permits, and local transport, all managed end-to-end\n- Culture enthusiasts and spiritual travelers looking to explore Spiti Valley’s Tibetan Buddhist heritage, ancient monasteries, and high-altitude Himalayan villages\n- Photography enthusiasts wanting to capture frozen waterfalls, snowy landscapes, and remote monasteries\n- First-time visitors wanting a hassle-free winter trip to Spiti\n- Travelers comfortable with cold weather and rugged mountain roads\n\n### **Top Destinations Covered in This Spiti Valley Road Trip**\n\n* **Shimla:** Known as the “Queen of Hills,” Shimla welcomes you with its colonial charm, bustling Mall Road, and breathtaking views from the Ridge. Explore the vibrant markets, enjoy local cafes, and soak in the cool mountain air as you prepare for the journey ahead.\n\n* **Chitkul:** Nestled at the end of the Baspa Valley and the last inhabited village on the old Hindustan-Tibet trade route, Chitkul offers unmatched tranquility and stunning views of the snow-capped Kinnaur Kailash range. Experience authentic Himalayan village life surrounded by pristine nature.\n\n* **Nako Lake:** On the way to Tabo, visit the serene [Nako Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/nako), set against the backdrop of quaint Nako village and the towering Himalayas. The lake is a spiritual and visual treat, often surrounded by snow-capped peaks and ancient monasteries.\n\n* **Tabo Monastery & Dhankar Village:** Explore [Tabo Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tabo-monastery), over 1,000 years old and often called the “Ajanta of the Himalayas” for its intricate murals and ancient Buddhist art. Nearby Dhankar Village and Gompa, perched on a cliff edge, provide breathtaking panoramic views of the Spiti Valley below and insights into ancient Himalayan culture.\n\n* **[Kaza](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kaza):** As the bustling hub and administrative center of Spiti Valley, Kaza blends Tibetan and Indian influences with vibrant markets, cozy cafés, and local culture. Nearby natural wonders such as Lingti waterfall add to the charm.\n\n* **Key Monastery:** The largest monastery in Spiti, [Key Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/key-monastery) stands tall on a hilltop, serving as a religious and educational center for lamas. Famous for its murals, thankas, rare manuscripts, and unique wind instruments, it is a spiritual highlight of the trip.\n\n* **[Komic](https://indiatour.live/attractions/komic), Langza & [Hikkim](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hikkim) Villages:** Visit Komic, one of the world’s highest motorable villages, offering stunning mountain vistas. Langza is famous for its giant Buddha statue overlooking the valley and its rich fossil deposits, revealing Spiti’s ancient marine past. Hikkim houses the world’s highest post office, a quirky and beloved spot for travelers.\n\n* **[Kibber](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kibber) & Chicham Bridge:** Kibber offers spectacular barren mountain landscapes dotted with ancient monasteries, embodying the stark beauty of Spiti. Chicham Bridge, Asia’s highest suspension bridge, adds an adrenaline rush and incredible photo opportunities.\n\n* **[Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake) (Moon Lake):** Known as the “Moon Lake,” Chandrataal is a pristine alpine lake nestled on the Samudra Tapu plateau. With crystal-clear waters reflecting the surrounding peaks, it is a favorite among trekkers and nature lovers. The campsite experience here is unforgettable under the Himalayan stars.\n\n* **Manali:** The final leg takes you to Manali, a vibrant hill station known for adventure activities like paragliding and river rafting, as well as cultural spots such as the Hadimba Devi Temple and the charming Old Manali marketplace. Manali perfectly combines thrills with relaxation to conclude your journey.",
