      "overviewText": "Spiti Valley is where everything slows down. Life in remote villages, ancient monasteries on cliff edges, icy rivers, and stretches of land that look nothing like the usual—this place feels like another planet. You’ll drive through [Atal Tunnel](https://indiatour.live/attractions/atal-tunnel), cross [Kunzum Pass](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kunzum-pass), and make your way to some of the highest motorable villages in the world.\n\nFrom the silence of Tabo and Dhankar monasteries to sending a postcard from Hikkim, spotting fossils in [Langza](https://indiatour.live/attractions/langza), and watching the stars over [Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake)—every stop hits different. It’s rugged, cold, and real.\n\nThis 10-day journey starts from Ahmedabad with a train ride to Chandigarh, and then continues by road through Manali and into Spiti.\n\n### Tour Details Summary\n\n**Duration:** 10 Days / 9 Nights\n\n**Start Point:** Ahmedabad (Gandhinagar) by Train\n\n**End Point:** Ahmedabad by Train via Chandigarh\n\n**Route:** Ahmedabad → Chandigarh → Manali → Kaza → Key, [Komic](https://indiatour.live/attractions/komic), Langza, [Hikkim](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hikkim) → Tabo & Dhankar → Chandrataal → Manali → Chandigarh → Ahmedabad\n\n**Transport:** Non-AC sleeper train (upgrade available), private vehicle for road trips, Volvo bus for some segments\n\n**Accommodation:** Hotels, homestays, campsites (especially at [Chandrataal](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake))\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast & Dinner included, Lunch & train food excluded\n\n**Highlights:** [Atal Tunnel](https://indiatour.live/attractions/atal-tunnel), Kunzum Pass, Tibetan monasteries, highest motorable villages, Asia’s highest suspension bridge, stunning high-altitude lakes, local cultural experiences, and panoramic mountain vistas\n\n**Inclusions:** Transport, accommodation, meals as per itinerary, permits, 24x7 support\n\n**Exclusions:** GST, lunches, any additional or emergency expenses\n\n### Who Should Book This Spiti Valley Tour\n\n- Backpackers and budget-conscious travelers\n- Travelers who want to experience **[Chandrataal Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake) camping** and **high-altitude Spiti villages**\n- Couples, friends, and small groups looking for a private, well-curated Spiti Valley tour—complete with train travel, meals, permits, and local transport, all managed end-to-end\n- Culture enthusiasts and spiritual travelers looking to explore Spiti Valley’s Tibetan Buddhist heritage, ancient monasteries, and high-altitude Himalayan villages\n- Photography enthusiasts wanting to capture frozen waterfalls, snowy landscapes, and remote monasteries\n- First-time visitors wanting a hassle-free winter trip to Spiti\n- Travelers comfortable with cold weather and rugged mountain roads\n\n### Top Destinations Covered in This Spiti Valley Tour\n\n- **Manali:** Gateway to Spiti, with charming temples, vibrant markets, and lush mountain scenery\n- **[Kaza](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kaza):** The main town of Spiti Valley, surrounded by vast landscapes and cultural richness\n- **[Key Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/key-monastery):** Largest Tibetan Buddhist monastery in Spiti, famous for its murals and religious significance\n- **Komic Village:** The world’s highest motorable village, home to the highest restaurant and monastery\n- **Langza Village:** Known as the Fossil Village, with a towering Buddha statue overlooking the valley\n- **Hikkim:** Home to the world’s highest post office, a must-visit quirky landmark\n- **Tabo Monastery:** A thousand-year-old monastery with ancient murals and spiritual significance\n- **[Dhankar Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/dhankar-monastery):** Perched on cliffs with panoramic valley views, a historical and spiritual gem\n- **Kibber:** Scenic village known for barren beauty and local monasteries\n- **[Chicham Bridge](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chicham-bridge):** Asia’s highest suspension bridge, offering breathtaking views\n- **Chandra Taal (Moon Lake):** A stunning high-altitude lake and trekker’s paradise\n- **Atal Tunnel & [Rohtang Pass](https://indiatour.live/attractions/rohtang-pass):** Engineering marvels connecting Lahaul and Spiti with Manali",
