      "routeSummary": "Shimla - Chandrataal -  Manali",
      "overviewText": "Spiti at its realest remote villages, high mountain passes, frozen lakes, and ancient monasteries tucked deep in the Himalayas. It’s cold, rugged, and far from the usual. But if you're up for it, it’s one of the most unforgettable experiences you’ll ever have.\n\nThe route takes you through Shimla, Chitkul, Kalpa, [Nako](https://indiatour.live/attractions/nako), [Tabo](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tabo-monastery), Dhankar, Kaza, Key Monastery, [Chicham Bridge](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chicham-bridge), and Chandratal Lake. Every place has its own pace, its own way of life. You’ll get to see how people survive—and thrive—in one of the harshest corners of India.\n\nWe’ve handled all the essentials—stay, food, local transport, permits, and logistics. You just show up with an open mind and let the mountains do the rest.\n\nThis 6-day itinerary starts from Delhi. Anyone can join the trip from Delhi.\n\n### Tour Details Summary\n\n**Duration:** 6 Days / 5 Nights\n\n**Start Point:** Delhi (ISBT Kashmiri Gate) by AC Volvo Bus\n\n**End Point:** Delhi via Manali by AC Volvo Bus\n\n**Route:** Delhi → [Shimla](https://indiatour.live/attractions/shimla) → Kalpa → Nako → Tabo → Dhankar → [Kaza](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kaza) → Key, Komic, Hikkim, [Langza](https://indiatour.live/attractions/langza) → Kibber → Chicham → Chandratal → Manali → Delhi\n\n**Transport:** AC Semi Sleeper Volvo (Delhi–Shimla & Manali–Delhi), private vehicle for road trip segments\n\n**Accommodation:** Hotels, homestays, and campsites (especially at Chandratal)\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast & Dinner included; lunch and food during travel excluded\n\n**Highlights:** Kalpa's apple orchards & Kinnaur Kailash views, Nako Lake, ancient monasteries (Tabo & Dhankar), Key Monastery, world’s highest villages (Komic & Hikkim), Langza Buddha statue, Asia’s highest Chicham Bridge, Chandratal Lake, thrilling mountain roads via Atal Tunnel or [Rohtang Pass](https://indiatour.live/attractions/rohtang-pass)\n\n**Inclusions:** Volvo tickets, private road trip vehicle, stays, meals as per itinerary, inner line permits, taxes, sightseeing, 24x7 support\n\n**Exclusions:** 5% GST, lunch, food during travel, any emergency costs or additional stays due to weather/roadblocks, personal expenses\n\n### Who Should Book This Spiti Valley Tour\n\n- Flexible start options available for travelers to join from Delhi\n- Backpackers and budget-conscious travelers\n- Travelers who want to experience **[Chandrataal Lake camping](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chandra-taal-lake)** and **high-altitude Spiti villages**\n- Anyone who wants to cover **Spiti Valley’s must-visit places** in a short duration\n- Couples, friends, and small groups looking for a private, well-curated Spiti Valley tour—complete with travel, meals, permits, and local transport, all managed end-to-end\n- Culture enthusiasts and spiritual travelers looking to explore Spiti Valley’s Tibetan Buddhist heritage, ancient monasteries, and high-altitude Himalayan villages\n- Photography enthusiasts wanting to capture frozen waterfalls, snowy landscapes, and remote monasteries\n- First-time visitors wanting a hassle-free winter trip to Spiti\n- Travelers comfortable with cold weather and rugged mountain roads\n\n### Top Destinations Covered in this Spiti Valley Tour\n\n- **[Shimla](https://indiatour.live/attractions/shimla):** The scenic hill station and gateway to Spiti, known for its colonial charm and panoramic views\n- **Kalpa:** Famous for apple orchards and spectacular views of the Kinnaur Kailash mountain range\n- **Tabo:** Home to the 1000-year-old Tabo Monastery, known for its ancient murals and spiritual significance\n- **Kaza:** The vibrant main town of Spiti Valley, serving as the perfect base to explore nearby villages and monasteries\n- **Key Monastery:** The largest Buddhist monastery in Spiti, renowned for its murals, thankas, and religious importance\n- **[Komic Village](https://indiatour.live/attractions/komic):** One of the world’s highest motorable villages with a serene monastery\n- **Langza:** Famous for its giant Buddha statue and rich fossil deposits\n- **Hikkim:** Known for the world’s highest post office\n- **[Kibber](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kibber):** A picturesque village with stunning barren landscapes and monasteries\n- **[Chicham Bridge](https://indiatour.live/attractions/chicham-bridge):** Asia’s highest suspension bridge, offering dramatic views\n- **Chandrataal Lake:** Also called Moon Lake, a breathtaking alpine lake and trekking hotspot\n- **Manali:** A popular hill station and the endpoint of the trip, with scenic beauty and adventure activities",
